<title>USA: Lockheed Martin wins U.S. census contract.</title>
<headline>Lockheed Martin wins U.S. census contract.</headline>
<dateline>GAITHERSBURG, Md. 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lockheed Martin Corp said its federal systems unit won a contract from the U.S. Commerce Department's census bureau to support the Year 2000 Decennial Census.</p>
<p>The initial value of the four-year contract is valued at about $49 million, the company said.</p>
<p>Lockheed Martin and its teammates, Electronic Data Systems Corp and CACI International Inc, will design and install a document imaging system that will digitally capture information from respondent census forms.</p>
